menu "Sample: hello world"

    config SAMPLE_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Network the WiFi feature joins first. Empty = the WiFi feature
            (and everything that needs it, such as Navidrome) reports
            "not configured" and does nothing.

            Keep credentials out of the tree: put them in an untracked
            sdkconfig.local.defaults next to sdkconfig.defaults, e.g.
                CONFIG_SAMPLE_WIFI_SSID="myssid"
                CONFIG_SAMPLE_WIFI_PASSWORD="mypassphrase"
            and build with
                idf.py -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.local.defaults" build
            (or set them with idf.py menuconfig; sdkconfig itself is not
            committed). Check that sdkconfig.local.defaults is gitignored
            before you fill it in.

    config SAMPLE_WIFI_SSID_ALT
        string "WiFi SSID (fallback)"
        default ""
        help
            Optional second network tried when the first one is unreachable
            (the 5 GHz name of the same router, for example). Same password.

    config SAMPLE_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password"
        default ""
        help
            WPA2 passphrase shared by both SSIDs. Empty = open network.

    config SAMPLE_NAVIDROME_URL
        string "Navidrome base URL"
        default ""
        help
            http(s)://host[:port] of a Navidrome (Subsonic API) server, no
            trailing slash. Empty = the Navidrome feature reports
            "not configured" and does nothing. See SAMPLE_WIFI_SSID for the
            sdkconfig.local.defaults recipe.

    config SAMPLE_NAVIDROME_USER
        string "Navidrome user"
        default ""
        help
            Login name. Must not need URL-encoding (plain ASCII letters and
            digits): it is pasted into the query string as is.

    config SAMPLE_NAVIDROME_PASSWORD
        string "Navidrome password"
        default ""
        help
            Cleartext password. The Subsonic API authenticates each request
            with md5(password + fresh salt), so the device has to hold the
            password itself; never commit a value here.

endmenu
